        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Prove&nbsp;\\(\\underset{x \\rightarrow - \\infty}{lim} \\frac{8}{\\left(x - 3\\right)^{2}} = 0\\).<br>\\(\\begin{matrix} |\\frac{8}{\\left(x - 3\\right)^{2}} - 0|  0 \\\\ \\frac{8}{\\epsilon}  x - 3 \\text{Positive} square root because x approaches negative infinity \\\\ - \\sqrt{\\frac{8}{\\epsilon}} + 3 > x Add . \\end{matrix}\\)<br>&nbsp;<br>So if&nbsp;\\(N =\\) \\(- \\sqrt{\\frac{8}{\\epsilon}} + 3\\), then&nbsp;\\(\\frac{8}{\\left(x - 3\\right)^{2}}\\) is within&nbsp;\\(\\epsilon\\) of 0."
        }
      ]
    },
